(D1 — Discrepancy 1 repro: loop expansion does NOT work with "any action that
 takes an argument" (LANGUAGE.md:312, and "works with any action" at :284).
 `append "ab" to sink` is legal on a buffer, and `append each n from 1 to 5
 to out` is legal on a list — but the two together are rejected: the
 expansion form of append silently loses the text-into-buffer capability the
 plain form has.
 The other refuted arms: `write each word from [...] to output.` →
 "Expected value to write" (BAS2-20.vox); `Set total to each number from 1
 to 3.` → "Expected a statement, got Each".
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D1.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Buffer append requires a buffer source: word
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
a buffer called sink is 64 bytes in size.
append each word from ["ab", "cd"] to sink.
print sink.
